-- title:
--   A rational place centred on a node of the full-level curve
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$ and a non-zero natural number $M'$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q} =$ `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, an intermediate field $k_0$ with $\mathbb Q \subseteq k_0 \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$, and $\pi_0 \in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$; write $A_0 = A\cap k_0$ for the comap of $A$ along $k_0 \to \overline{\mathbb Q}$. Assume $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$, is Henselian local, has algebraically closed residue field, and that every $a\in A$ differs from some element of $A_0$ by an element of the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $F$ be the intermediate field `fieldBar q M'` of $\overline{\mathbb Q} \subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}(\overline{\mathbb Q})$, an algebra over $k_0$ through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. Let $F_0$ be an intermediate field of $F$ over $k_0$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q}\cdot F_0 = F$ (the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is everything) and satisfying the linear disjointness condition: for every finite-dimensional intermediate field $K'$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ over $k_0$, every finite family $c_i \in \overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every family $a_i$ in the join of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, the relation $\sum_i c_i a_i = 0$ forces all $a_i = 0$. Let $O$ be a Noetherian local subring of $F_0$ such that, for $x\in k_0$, $x \in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ lies in $O$; such that every $f \in O$ may be written as the sum of (the image of) an element of $A_0$ and a non-unit of $O$; and such that $F_0$ is the fraction field of $O$, in the sense that every $f\in F_0$ satisfies $fh = g$ for some $g, h \in O$ with $h \neq 0$. Finally let $E_0 \geq 1$, assume the image of $\pi_0$ lies in $O$, and let $\iota_O$ be a ring isomorphism from the adic completion of $O$ at its maximal ideal onto `UVCrossingModel` of the adic completion $\widehat{A_0}$ of $A_0$ at its maximal ideal with parameter the $E_0$-th power of the image of $\pi_0$, that is, the quotient of the two-variable power series ring over $\widehat{A_0}$ by the ideal `uvCrossingIdeal`, and assume $\iota_O$ carries the image in $\widehat O$ of each element of $A_0 \subseteq O$ to the class `const` of the corresponding constant power series. The conclusion is that there exists a place $P$ of $F$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, that is, a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, different from $F$ and a principal ideal ring, such that (i) every element of $O$ lies in the valuation subring of $P$, and (ii) for every non-unit $f$ of $O$ the value $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ lies in $A$ and in fact in the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   This is the existence statement that a node of the level-field model, read inside the full-level modular function field, is the reduction of an algebraic point: the annulus around the node carries a $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-rational place whose centre is the node. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_baseRationalNodeRing_input_of_node_ends_nodePlaces`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_baseRationalNodeRing_input_of_node_ends_nodePlaces) and its prime-level variant, where the remaining content is transport of structure.
